2026-08-15T17:20:06.6397828Z   PR_BODY: ## Summary

- Treat a self-development-policy-ineligible automatic release as a clean
  deferral while retaining the strict manual release gate.
- Build the all-feature macOS nextest archive once, then fan it out to three
  bounded partition runners instead of compiling the graph three times.
- Add one fail-closed gate that discovers and audits every committed Bun/npm
  lock; upgrade DOMPurify and the vulnerable Puppeteer extraction chains until
  all five live locks report zero advisories.
- Remove misleading Gemini true-color/project-lock warnings and Bun lifecycle
  noise, and rename archived manifests so Dependency Graph cannot treat
  historical evidence as live applications.
- Preserve the complete issue/PR/CI evidence, reconstructed timeline, nine
  requirements, root-cause ledger, template comparison, and upstream reports.

## Root causes and reproduction

The issue-listed baseline contained one real Auto Release failure, which
Pipeline Status correctly propagated. The new hard self-development gate ran
after an immutable release cycle without a qualifying PR, so every future
automatic run would stay red even though retrying could not change eligibility.
The macOS warnings were also real: all three nextest slices rebuilt the same
all-feature graph before partitioning. Install-time npm audit output did not
fail CI, leaving four vulnerable dependency surfaces behind an apparent green
run.

The tests-first commit `769c1eac` captures the seven initial failures. The
canonical evidence index contains all twelve named baseline run logs, all five
initial PR run logs, run/job/artifact metadata, 66 check-annotation responses,
all three PR discussion surfaces, and the red/green reproduction:

[`dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/README.md`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-1014-fa915643117e/dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/README.md)

## Verification

- `cargo test --test unit -- ci_cd::issue_1014` — 12/12 pass
- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features`
- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo check --examples --all-features`
- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo test --all-features --verbose` — 2,804 library
  tests plus every integration binary pass
- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo test --doc --all-features --verbose`
- `bash scripts/check-javascript-dependencies.sh` — all five locks clean
- desktop tests — 140/140; VS Code tests — 51/51; web tests — 75/75 plus build
- actionlint with the repository's documented `queue` schema exception
- formatting, diff whitespace, shell syntax, changelog, static policies, and
  committed-range secret scan (351 files)

Full local output is retained under
`dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/local-tests/`. Fresh GitHub runs are verified by
timestamp and exact head SHA before this draft is marked ready.

## Upstream reports

- [Gemini CLI #28826](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/28826)
